I traced the actual architecture. Two distinct problems, both real:

**1. Blast and Gravity share one global `[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]` Map** (`[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]`). It's not per-mode state — it's a single object whose behavior branches on `[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO] === 'gravity'`. So placing pieces in Blast and later entering Gravity (or vice versa) operates on the same underlying grid.

**2. Three modes reset unconditionally on every `init()`:** Blast, Gravity, and Snake all call `this.reset()` (which for Blast/Gravity includes `[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO].clear()`) every time you switch into them — win/loss progress, piece queue, everything, gone on every visit. Sandbox, [REDACTED_PERSON], Compose, and Melody already do this right (state survives revisits; [REDACTED_PERSON]'s remaining bug was the async-fetch race I just fixed).

**Plan:**
- Give Blast and Gravity each their own board (`[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]` / `[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]`, dropping the `[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]` branching in `board.js` in favor of two independent instances built from one factory).
- Stop calling `reset()` from `init()` in Blast/Gravity/Snake — only reset on first-ever entry or an explicit "New Game"/reset button click (which already exist), so switching away and back resumes exactly where you left off, timers paused via existing `cleanup()`.
- Update the handful of call sites in `[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]`/`[REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]` that reference the global `Board` to use the right mode's instance.
- Regression test: place in Blast, switch to Gravity, confirm Gravity's board is empty and Blast's placement wasn't touched; and confirm switching away/back to Blast preserves its board and score.

Then, separately: add a 💾 Save-As icon button to [REDACTED_PERSON]'s controls (matching Compose's), saving the current automaton (rule/state/cells/tempo) as YAML to the remembered local folder, with the same folder-picker/download-fallback pattern Compose/Melody already use via `js/midi-folder.js`.

